								@* a11y + dead link. This icon-only control was the ONLY source of the 132 link-name
								   findings: no text, no title, no aria-label — announced simply as "link".
								   It was also still pointing at "authentication/layouts/corporate/sign-in.html", a
								   Metronic DEMO TEMPLATE PATH that does not exist in this application, so the control
								   404'd. Naming a broken link would have made it worse: a screen-reader user would be
								   told "Sign out" and taken nowhere.
								   Both halves are fixed together. The href now targets the same action the user menu
								   already uses (Account/Logout, a few lines above), and the name comes from
								   SharedResources.Logout so it is localized exactly like that menu item. The glyph is
								   decorative and hidden from assistive technology. *@
								<!--begin::Link-->
