		@* METRONIC DEMO SCAFFOLDING REMOVED — dead template content, not CrossBuy functionality.

		   Removed here: the Drawers block (activities log, chat messenger, shopping cart) and the Modals block
		   (upgrade plan, view users, users search, invite friends) — 3,437 lines of unreachable Metronic sample
		   markup carrying 126 interactive elements.

		   WHY REMOVED RATHER THAN LABELLED. Each drawer declared data-kt-drawer-toggle="#kt_activities_toggle" /
		   "#kt_drawer_chat_toggle" / "#kt_drawer_shopping_cart_toggle", and NO element with any of those ids
		   existed anywhere in the application — so no user could ever open them. The four modals were reachable
		   only from links inside the dead chat drawer itself. The whole graph was self-referential demo content
		   with zero inbound references from real CrossBuy code (verified across every view and script).

		   Those 126 elements were the source of the remaining shared-shell axe findings: icon-only controls with
		   no accessible name, and links to Metronic demo destinations (apps/ecommerce/…, apps/inbox/…,
		   account/overview.html) that 404 in this product. Giving them aria-labels would have made the audit
		   green while leaving a user — especially a screen-reader user — able to reach controls that go nowhere.
		   Deleting scaffolding nobody can open is the honest fix; naming it is not.

		   KEPT: the Scrolltop control below, which is a real, reachable utility. *@
